nt as PYI_INSPECT is): 'q' for -q, 'E' for -E, 'I' for -I; sys.flags' quiet, ignore_environment and"] [99 1 "// isolated (asyncio's REPL reads quiet for its banner and ignore_environment for PYTHONSTARTUP)."] [113 1 "// startInspect is -i (bin/pyi python's PYI_INSPECT, queue 289, read once and removed from the environment as"] [114 1 "// PYI_SAFE_PATH is): 0 without it, 1 for -i, 2 for -i with no code to run (CPython's REPL on stdin, its banner but"] [115 1 "// under -q). PYTHONINSPECT at start (but under -E or -I) sets sys.flags.inspect, not interactive, as config's inspect."] [138 1 "// inspectAfter is pymain_repl's test (Modules/main.c): the REPL after the main module when -i was given or"] [139 1 "// PYTHONINSPECT is set (at start, or in the environment the program leaves), stdin a terminal or -i given."] [148 1 "// endMain is the main module's end with its status: Py_FinalizeEx's, or under -i the REPL on stdin in __main__'s"] [149 1 "// namespace (pymain_repl; the module's exception, SystemExit's too, printed before it), whose status is the run's."] [158 2 "// pymain_set_inspect(config, 0) before the REPL: sys.flags.inspect 0 in it (sys made first: an empty main module"] [159 2 "// has not made it)"] [165 3 "// no code to run: the REPL is the run, its __main__ the empty stdin module's without a __file__"] [167 3 "// and with what pylifecycle's add_main_module gives it (queue 298, test_pyrepl's globals tests): __package__ and"] [168 3 "// __spec__ None, __loader__ importlib's BuiltinImporter"] [173 21 "// stderr unbuffered, as CPython's: the banner before the hook's and _pyrepl's imports (queue 298)"] [180 2 "// sys.__interactivehook__ (pymain_run_interactive_hook; queue 298: site's register_readline, the history file)"] [184 2 "// on a terminal, _pyrepl (pymain_run_pyrepl; queue 298): pythonstartup after code (pymain_repl), not on stdin's run"] [185 2 "// (pymain_run_stdin ran the startup file above)"] [192 1 "// mainModuleDefaults gives __main__'s namespace g of a run with no code the names CPython's __main__ starts with"] [193 1 "// (add_main_module, Python/pylifecycle.c): __package__ and __spec__ None, __loader__ BuiltinImporter, each when absent."] [215 1 "// runInteractiveHook is pymain_run_interactive_hook (Modules/main.c; queue 298), before the REPL: sys.__interactivehook__"] [216 1 "// called when sys has one (site's register_readline: readline's or _pyrepl's history file read, its write at exit"] [217 1 "// registered); an error is \"Failed calling sys.__interactivehook__\" and printed, the session going on, but SystemExit,"] [218 1 "// whose status ends the run (exit true), as pymain_err_print."] [223 2 "// site, which CPython imports at start (pyi does not): imported here, before the REPL, so that its main sets the hook"] [224 2 "// (enablerlcompleter, but under -I)"] [248 1 "// runStartup is pymain_run_startup (Modules/main.c; queue 293), before the REPL on stdin when there is no code to run:"] [249 1 "// the file PYTHONSTARTUP names (not under -E or -I) run in __main__'s namespace g as _PyRun_SimpleFileObject runs it,"] [250 1 "// its __file__ set for the run, an error printed (sys.excepthook) and the session going on; SystemExit ends the run"] [251 1 "// with its status (exit true), as PyErr_Print's handle_system_exit; a file that does not open: \"Could not open"] [252 1 "// PYTHONSTARTUP\" and its OSError printed."] [295 1 "// cModeFile is the file bin/pyi python writes -c's code into (queue 220): run as CPython runs -c, its code's file"] [296 1 "// \"<string>\", no __file__, sys.path[0] \"\"."] [299 1 "// mModeFile and stdinModeFile are the files bin/pyi python writes for -m and for a program read from stdin (queue 250)."] [305 1 "// startSafePath is -P (safe_path) as bin/pyi python's command line gave it (PYI_SAFE_PATH: 1 under -P or -I, 0"] [306 1 "// without, read once and removed from the environment as PYI_IGNORE_ENV is); -1 when not run by bin/pyi python (bin/pyi"] [307 1 "// run's programs and the check's driver, whose sys.flags.safe_path is the reference driver's -P)."] [328 1 "// ExecModule runs a module's code object as the module name (its namespace's __name__), returning"] [329 1 "// the module, or the uncaught exception."] [334 1 "// PrintException writes an uncaught exception as CPython's default excepthook does"] [335 1 "// (Lib/traceback.py's format): the chain first (__cause__, else __context__ unless suppressed), each"] [336 1 "// with its traceback (the file, line and function, and the source line when the file reads) and"] [337 1 "// \"Type: text\", a SyntaxError's location and caret, the notes. Carets under expressions are not"] [338 1 "// printed (PY5b: a recorded difference)."] [339 1 "//"] [340 1 "// The text goes to sys.stderr (PyErr_Display's file): the process's standard error while sys.stderr is"] [341 1 "// the one it started with, else the text is written by sys.stderr.write and flushed (support.captured_stderr),"] [342 1 "// nothing when sys.stderr is None or missing, write's errors ignored."] [356 1 "// PrintUncaught is PyErr_Print (Python/pythonrun.c's _PyErr_PrintEx with set_sys_last_vars, queue 223): an uncaught"] [357 1 "// exception, not SystemExit, stored as sys.last_exc, last_type, last_value and last_traceback, then given to"] [358 1 "// sys.excepthook(type, value, traceback); \"sys.excepthook is missing\" and the display when it is absent or None; when"] [359 1 "// the hook raises, \"Error in sys.excepthook:\", that error's display, then \"Original exception was:\" and the original's."] [366 22 "// after the main module's run: the hook runs on the main thread"] [394 1 "// registerCode is run_mod's interactive source (Python/pythonrun.c, queue 223): -c's code and its nested code objects"] [395 1 "// registered by linecache._register_code(code, source, name), so traceback's display shows -c's lines; an error dropped."] [409 1 "// displayByTraceback is _PyErr_Display's first way (Python/pythonrun.c, queue 223): the stdlib's"] [410 1 "// traceback._print_exception_bltin(exc), Lib/traceback.py's display with its caret lines (PEP 657's positions,"] [411 1 "// co_positions), chains, groups and notes; false when the module or its function is missing or the call raised (the"] [412 1 "// error dropped, as PyErr_Clear), the caller then printing the Go display (print_exception_recursive's fallback)."] [413 1 "// Not while traceback itself is being imported or displaying (a second error then printed by the fallback)."] [445 1 "// writeStderr writes text to sys.stderr: in.Stderr when it is the original stream."] [485 4 "// at shutdown CPython's display reads no source (the import of io fails: queue 253)"] [494 1 "// FormatExceptionOnly is traceback.format_exception_only's text: a SyntaxError's location, source"] [495 1 "// line and caret, then \"Type: text\" (the type qualified by its module unless builtins), then the notes."] [500 23 "// traceback's stype: the module unless __main__ or builtins"] [504 3 "// str(exc) (traceback's _safe_string): a class's own __str__"] [584 1 "// RegisterSource gives sourceLine the text of a source that is no file (\"<stdin>\", \"<string>\"): the"] [585 1 "// REPL's statements, as linecache keeps them (PY5e's REQUEST, part 2a). A later text replaces it."] [590 1 "// sourceLine is the stripped text of line n of the file, \"\" when it does not read (linecache)."] [612 1 "// RunModule reads a module's IR (arbace.python.compile's code object as pr-str prints it) and runs it"] [613 1 "// as __main__ with file as __file__, on the process's stdout and stderr; the exit status: 0, 1 for an"] [614 1 "// uncaught exception (its traceback on stderr), SystemExit's code. bin/pyi run calls it."] [615 1 "// mainSourceError is the main file's decoding error as the tokenizer reports a file it reads, the file named"] [616 1 "// (helpers.c's \" in file FILE\", as arbace.python.run/error-answer gives pyi on goi's; queue 284: the compiled"] [617 1 "// launcher's main module, which RunModule